{
    /* Jacobi iteration for the tridiagonal system

           4·x[i] + x[i-1] + x[i+1] = b[i],   x = 0 outside the grid.

       Each sweep reads the whole previous X — a Jacobi step — and `⇒` repeats
       it until no cell moves by more than 𝜏 (--tau) or --max-iter sweeps have
       run. The update's coefficients on X sum to 1/2, so the compiler proves
       the iteration contracts in the ∞-norm: it converges from any start.

         rhoc examples/jacobi.rho --tau 1e-12 --max-iter 200
    */
    INPUT:◯ □ 64 1
    INPUT → X
    ((INPUT - (▷X + ▽X)) / 4.0) ⇒ X
    X → =
}
